{"name":"Grand Piano","hex":"#d8d0bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grand piano","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large piano in which the strings are strung horizontally in a heavy frame shaped like a harp."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grand_piano"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grand Piano (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Grand Piano is a 2013 Spanish English-language thriller film directed by Eugenio Mira, written by Damien Chazelle, and starring Elijah Wood and John Cusack. The film is about a once-promising pianist returning for a comeback performance, only to be the target of a sniper who will kill him if he plays one wrong note. The film premiered at Fantastic Fest on 20 September 2013 and was given a VOD release on 30 January 2014. It was given a limited release in American theatres on 7 March. Grand Piano was Alex Winter's first non-cameo film role since 1993's Freaked."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/Grand_Piano_Official_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Piano_(film)","wikidata":"Q3113698"},{"title":"Grand Piano (Narada Anniversary Collection)","blocks":[{"text":"Grand Piano is a 1997 compilation by Narada. It peaked at No. 10 on Billboard's Top New Age album charts in the same year."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/Naradagrandpiano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Piano_(Narada_Anniversary_Collection)","wikidata":"Q5594882"},{"title":"Piano","blocks":[{"text":"A piano is a keyboard instrument that produces sound when its keys are pressed, activating an action mechanism where hammers strike strings. Modern pianos have a row of 88 black and white keys—with the exception of the Bosendörfer and Stuart & Sons pianos—and tuned to a chromatic scale in equal temperament. A musician who specializes in piano is called a pianist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Steinway_Vienna_002.JPG/330px-Steinway_Vienna_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piano","wikidata":"Q5994"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg/500px-Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg/500px-Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiano_droit_Weinbach_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/PianoRange.tif/lossy-page1-500px-PianoRange.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/PianoRange.tif/lossy-page1-500px-PianoRange.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APianoRange.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg/500px-CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg/1280px-CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/